From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:07:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: route SM8750 IPP frames through the TFE
 pixel pipeline

Configure the CSID IPP port for the TFE pixel path: set the context
index and the Bayer order (CAMIF_FRAME_CFG[26:24], from the sink media
bus code) the TFE demosaics with, and issue a register update (RUP)
along with the address update on the IPP port so that ISP settings
changed while streaming latch on the next frame.

Port the existing Piano PIX path to the v7 CSID/VFE 980 backends.
Keep the v7 RDI route on other machines and select Piano-specific VFE
resources, media pads and Bayer clocks only on Xiaomi Piano.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/6f3dc4ced0ed98f533f18f7e066f2cfcc05d1672
Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <bluseliu50@gmail.com>

Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/dc4d2e2737caf82b7ee59114c7110707c877085a

Run the SM8750 TFE pixel (PIX) line: the Bayer clocks of each TFE,
the 980 pixel formats, and an image pipeline programmed from kernel
defaults: black level and white balance in the 14-bit Bayer stage,
demosaic, an sRGB gamma LUT (with an optional S-curve blend), BT.601
colour transform, MN downscaling from the sink compose rectangle and
crop/round to 8-bit NV12.

The PIX subdev exposes the white balance gains, digital gain,
saturation, contrast and a driver-private colour correction matrix
(folded into the colour transform) as controls; exposure, white
balance and focus loops are left to userspace. A debugfs bring-up aid
(camss_isp/) applies register scripts at pixel-path start and gives
live register access while the path streams.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <bluseliu50@gmail.com>

Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/84cb707e0a81e343f4c558c59858032e60eaeb5b

Keep frame diagnostics and omit the short-lived raw-register debugfs interface.
